 are located. The lighting is bright enough to distinguish the golden color of the trim from the deep blue stage floor and the darker audience seating. Even in frames with slightly dimmer ambient lighting (e.g., 25–30), the golden decorations remain clearly identifiable due to their reflective surface and contrast with surrounding elements.\n\n---\n\n**Frames 7–9:**\n\nThese frames are closer shots of the stage, focusing on the podium and seated dignitaries. The front edge of the stage is visible at the bottom of the frame, and it is decorated with floral arrangements (yellow and orange flowers) rather than the ornate trim seen in the wide shots. However, the ornate golden trim is still visible along the side edges of the stage in these frames.\n\n---\n\n**Frames 17–20:**\n\nThese are close-ups of orchestra members. The stage edge is not visible in these frames.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion on Color of Stage Edge Decorations:**\n\nBased on consistent visual evidence across multiple frames (1–6, 10–16, 21–30), the decorations on the edge of the stage are **gold** in color.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question “What color is the decoration on the edge of the stage?” is **not C. Black**.\n\nThe correct choice, based on typical 0-indexing (A=0, B=1, C=2, D=3), would be:\n\n- **A. Gold** (if A corresponds to Gold)\n- Or if the options are: A. White, B. Blue, C. Black, D. Gold → then **D. Gold**\n\nSince the question specifically asks whether **C. Black** is correct, the answer is:\n\n> **No, C. Black is not correct. The decorations on the stage edge are clearly gold.**\n\n--- \n\n✅ Final Answer: **C. Black is incorrect. The decorations are gold.**'}, {'batch_start': 90, 'batch_end': 112, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/lDlA7cfNk8A/frames/frame_4355.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/lDlA7cfNk8A/frames/frame_4356.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/lDlA7cfNk8A/frames/frame_4357.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/lDlA7c