d with ornate, gilded decorations. These appear to be sculpted or molded elements, possibly floral or scrollwork in design, consistent with the grand, classical architecture of the Stockholm Concert Hall.\n\n---\n\n**3) What color are the decorations on the stage edge?**\n\n✅ **Gold.** Across all frames where the stage edge is visible (especially 1–6, 19–20, 24–30), the decorations are consistently illuminated and appear to be **gold or gilded**. The lighting enhances their metallic sheen, and they contrast sharply with the dark blue stage floor and the dark wood or fabric of the surrounding architecture.\n\nThis is clearly visible in the wide shots where the stage front is lit, such as Frame 1, Frame 24, and Frame 30.\n\n---\n\n**4) Is the lighting sufficient to clearly identify colors?**\n\n✅ **Yes.** The stage is well-lit, especially along its edges, with spotlights and ambient hall lighting designed to highlight the ceremony’s grandeur. The gold color of the decorations is vivid and unmistakable under this illumination. Even in darker frames (e.g., Frame 24), the reflective quality of the gold is apparent.\n\n---\n\n**Final Determination:**\n\nThe question asks whether answer **'C. Black'** is correct for “What color is the decoration on the edge of the stage?”\n\n❌ **No, 'C. Black' is not correct.**\n\nThe decorations on the stage edge are **gold**, not black. The visual evidence across multiple frames is consistent: the ornate trim along the stage perimeter is gilded and clearly visible as gold under the stage lighting.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\n- **Stage edge clearly visible?** Yes.\n- **Decorations present?** Yes.\n- **Color of decorations?** Gold.\n- **Lighting sufficient to identify color?** Yes.\n- **Is 'C. Black' correct?** ❌ No. The correct color is **Gold**.\n\n---"}, {'batch_start': 60, 'batch_end': 90, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/lDlA7cfNk8A/frames/frame_3002.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/lDlA7cfNk8A/fra